{"id":"2011b8f0fd783dadc2d71359487b2b5d67a82744","axis":"silent","repo":"vllm-project/vllm","sha":"2011b8f0fd783dadc2d71359487b2b5d67a82744","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"rust/README.md","lines":["@@ -132,8 +132,8 @@ For external load balancing, start one `vllm-rs serve` per rank with `--data-par"," "," ### Engine-free renderer"," ","-`vllm-rs render` serves text-only request preprocessing without starting or","-connecting to a Python inference engine:","+`vllm-rs render` serves request preprocessing without starting or connecting","+to a Python inference engine:"," "," ```bash"," cargo run --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml -p vllm-cmd --release -- \\","@@ -142,8 +142,28 @@ cargo run --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml -p vllm-cmd --release -- \\"," ```"," "," It exposes `/v1/chat/completions/render` and `/v1/completions/render`. Only","-tokenizer and model configuration files are loaded; model weights, PyTorch,","-and vLLM kernels are not required.","+tokenizer, model and processor configuration files are loaded; model weights,","+PyTorch, and vLLM kernels are not required.","+","+For multimodal models, chat render fetches and preprocesses images, video and","+audio, and returns them as the `features` object that `/inference/v1/generate`","+accepts, in the format the Python render API uses. The tensors are produced in","+`--dtype`, which must match the engine's: `auto` (the default) follows the","+model config, running float32 checkpoints in bfloat16 like vLLM, but unlike","+vLLM it does not look at the weights or the GPU, so pass the engine's dtype","+when they decide it. Set `--max-model-len` to the engine's too: some image","+processors size images to fit the context. Large images make `features` big;","+the generate server may need `VLLM_HTTP_MAX_REQUEST_BODY_SIZE` raised above","+its 32 MiB default to accept them. Set","+`\"mm_payload\": \"none\"` on a render request to get only item hashes and","+placeholder ranges, for example for cache-aware routing; such a response cannot","+be sent to generate. Pass `--language-model-only` to skip multimodal","+processing, and set `--limit-mm-per-prompt` to the engine's limits so that","+render rejects the same requests.","+","+Pass `--lora-modules name=path ...` to accept LoRA adapter names as the request","+`model`; rendering does not load the adapter weights, and the adapter name is","+passed through to generate."," "," To serve HTTPS, pass `--ssl-certfile`. If the certificate and private key are"," in separate files, pass `--ssl-keyfile` for the key; otherwise the key is read from"],"additions":24,"deletions":4,"truncated":false},{"path":"rust/src/chat/src/backend/hf.rs","lines":["@@ -494,7 +494,7 @@ mod tests {","             r#\"{\"model_type\":\"deepseek_v4\"}\"#,","             \"{}\",","         );","-        let processor = crate::ChatRequestProcessor::render_only(Arc::new(backend))","+        let processor = crate::ChatRequestProcessor::new(Arc::new(backend), None, None)","             .with_reasoning_effort_map([(\"high\".to_string(), \"max\".to_string())].into());"," ","         let mut request = request_with_user_text(\"hello\");","@@ -535,7 +535,7 @@ mod tests {","             let backend = backend_for_selection(Auto, config_json, TOKENIZER_CONFIG);","             let mut request = request_with_user_text(\"hello\");","             request.chat_options.chat_template = Some(TEMPLATE.to_string());","-            crate::ChatRequestProcessor::render_only(Arc::new(backend))","+            crate::ChatRequestProcessor::new(Arc::new(backend), None, None)","                 .prepare_for_tokenization(request)","                 .await","                 .unwrap_err()"],"additions":2,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"rust/src/chat/src/lib.rs","lines":["@@ -77,11 +77,11 @@ use vllm_text::{Prompt, TextLlm, TextRequest, TextRequestProcessor};"," /// Chat request preparation shared by inference and render-only frontends."," pub struct ChatRequestProcessor {","     backend: DynChatBac